  "guideWelcomeIntro": "Short recipes to get going. Each one links to a clip of the gesture on the website.",
  "guideChangelogExpand": "What's new in this version",
  "guideMidiHardwareStep1": "Plug the controller in, or switch on the Bluetooth one.",
  "guideMidiHardwareStep2": "Open Preferences with the gear icon. Under MIDI Connection, tap Connect MIDI Device and pick it.",
  "guideMidiCcMappings": "Map knobs and pads",
  "guideMidiCcMappingsBody": "For a module's controls: tap the sliders icon at the top of the module, tap Learn next to a control, then move a knob or press a pad.\nFor actions that concern the whole app (looper, transport, channel swap and more): open Preferences, then CC Mapping Preferences, then Add Mapping.",
  "guideMidiTipSplit": "Many controllers can split their keys into two zones on different MIDI channels, for example bass in the left hand and melody in the right.",
  "guideAndroidUsbLimitation": "Android keeps only one USB audio device at a time. If plugging in a USB microphone silences your USB headphones or sound card, turn on Direct USB output in Preferences, under Audio Output.",
