  "ampIrRejected": "The amp could not use this IR.",
  "guideRiffTitle": "Riff, the modelled guitar",
  "guideRiffBody": "Riff is an electric guitar modelled string by string. It has no keys: cable a keyboard's MIDI OUT into its MIDI IN, or play it from a controller on its MIDI channel.\nClose notes go to separate strings, so they ring together. With Legato on, a note close to the previous one hammers on or pulls off on the same string. Overlap does the same only when you press a key before letting go of the last one.\nThe pitch wheel bends, the mod wheel adds vibrato, the sustain pedal lets strings ring. Feedback makes held strings bloom into a harmonic, like in front of an amp.\nPalm mute, Pick position, Tone and the pickup selector change strings that are already ringing: map them to a pedal or a knob with Learn and play them like a guitarist's hands. For crunch and distortion, cable Riff into the Amp.",
  "guideAmpTitle": "Amp and cabinet IRs",
  "guideAmpBody": "The Amp has three sections you can switch on and off, by hand or with a footswitch: a Drive pedal (Overdrive or Distortion), the amp itself (Gain, Bass, Middle, Treble) and the speaker cabinet.\nThe cabinet shapes most of a guitar sound. Besides the three built-in ones, the Amp can play an impulse response (IR), a recording of a real cabinet: tap Load IR under the Amp and pick a .wav file. It is saved in your project; the cross next to its name removes it.",
  "guideAmpIrSourcesTitle": "Where to find free cabinet IRs",
