  "guideTabRehearsals": "Rehearsals",
  "@guideTabRehearsals": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalIntroTitle": "Rehearsing together",
  "@guideRehearsalIntroTitle": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalIntroBody": "The Rehearse tab is for a band learning a tune. Everyone records their own part over a shared click, on their own device, and every device ends up with all the parts.\n\nNothing is uploaded anywhere. The devices talk straight to each other, so a rehearsal works in a room with no internet at all.",
  "@guideRehearsalIntroBody": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalStartTitle": "Starting a tune",
  "@guideRehearsalStartTitle": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalStartBody": "Start a tune, give it a name, and say what you play. Set the tempo and the time signature, or tap the beat if you would rather feel it than count it.\n\nTo play along to a recording, import it as the master track: MP3, FLAC and WAV everywhere, and on Android also M4A, AAC and the sound of a video. Then tap along to the beat and drag the marker onto the first downbeat, so the bars line up with the music. The click then switches off: the recording sets the tempo.",
  "@guideRehearsalStartBody": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalRecordTitle": "Recording your part",
  "@guideRehearsalRecordTitle": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalRecordBody": "Add a part for your instrument and press record. A count-in plays first, two bars by default, and recording starts on the downbeat.\n\nEvery device takes a moment to play sound and another to record it, which would put your take late against the others. The app measures that delay on your device and moves your take back by it, so what you played on the beat lands on the beat. Measure it once with Calibrate in the tune, or from Preferences, and again when you change headphones or switch to a Bluetooth speaker: the delay belongs to the gear, not to the tune.\n\nYou record your own parts and nobody else's. Yours can be re-recorded or deleted as often as you like.",
  "@guideRehearsalRecordBody": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalMonitoringNote": "Record with headphones, or with an external microphone kept away from the speaker. Through the built-in speaker, the microphone hears the click and the parts already recorded, and they all end up in your take.",
  "@guideRehearsalMonitoringNote": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab: info box under Recording."
  },
  "guideRehearsalShareTitle": "Getting the band together",
  "@guideRehearsalShareTitle": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalShareBody": "The first time, one person opens the tune and taps the share icon; the others join from the Rehearse tab, with Join a tune: on a phone they scan the code, on a computer they paste the link. After that, the devices know each other: opening the same tune is enough, and they find each other within a few seconds.\n\nA dot next to each part shows whether its player is connected. What you record reaches everyone in the room as soon as you stop, and what you missed while away arrives the next time you are all together.",
  "@guideRehearsalShareBody": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalHotspotTitle": "When there is no Wi-Fi",
  "@guideRehearsalHotspotTitle": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalHotspotBody": "Everyone has to be on the same network. Phones on mobile data cannot see each other, and rehearsal rooms rarely have usable Wi-Fi, so one person makes the network:\n\n1. One phone turns on its personal hotspot, in the phone's own settings (usually under Connections or Network).\n2. Everyone else joins that hotspot from their Wi-Fi settings, like any network.\n3. Everyone opens the tune. The devices find each other within a few seconds.\n\nIt does not have to be the same person every time: if the usual host is away, anybody else turns theirs on and the rest join it. There is nothing to scan again.",
  "@guideRehearsalHotspotBody": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
  "guideRehearsalHotspotNote": "Sharing parts uses no mobile data: it never leaves the room. Some phones ask to turn mobile data on before sharing a hotspot, but the rehearsal itself does not use any.",
  "@guideRehearsalHotspotNote": {
    "description": "User guide, Rehearsals tab."
  },
