  "guideRulesTitle": "How sound moves between modules",
  "guideRulesIntro": "Tap the cable icon at the top of the rack to see the back of your modules. That is where you connect them with cables.",
  "guideRuleInstrument": "An instrument plays through the speakers on its own. You do not need a cable to hear it.",
  "guideRuleColours": "Yellow cables carry notes (MIDI), from a keyboard to an instrument. Red and white cables carry sound, left and right.",
  "guideRuleEffect": "To put an effect after an instrument, cable the instrument's AUDIO OUT L and R into the effect's AUDIO IN L and R. What comes out of the effect goes to the speakers.",
  "guideRuleDraw": "To draw a cable, long-press a socket and drag it to another one. Sockets that accept it light up while you drag.",
  "guideWatchClip": "Watch the clip",
  "guideRecipeScaleTitle": "Play in a scale",
  "guideRecipeScaleSteps": "Every new project has a keyboard and a Xen module.\nHold a key and tap a scale, for example Blues. Xen switches on, and the key you hold becomes the root note.\nOpen Family for other traditions: maqamat, ragas, Japanese scales and more.",
  "guideRecipeScaleResult": "Grey keys are outside the scale: press one and you hear the nearest note that fits.",
  "guideRecipeEffectTitle": "Add an effect to your keyboard",
  "guideRecipeEffectSteps": "Tap + and pick an effect, for example Reverb.\nTap the cable icon at the top.\nLong-press the keyboard's red AUDIO OUT L and drag it to the effect's AUDIO IN L. Then the white R to R.\nTap the back arrow and play.",
  "guideRecipeEffectResult": "You hear the keyboard through the effect. Turn its knobs to change the sound.",
  "guideRecipeRemoveTitle": "Remove a cable or a module",
  "guideRecipeRemoveSteps": "A cable: in the cable view, tap the small ✕ in the middle of the cable, then Disconnect.\nA module: tap the bin icon at the top of the module, then Remove. Its cables go with it.",
  "guideRecipeRemoveResult": "",
  "guideRecipeGuitarTitle": "Play the guitar from the keyboard",
  "guideRecipeGuitarSteps": "Tap + and pick Riff.\nIn the cable view, drag the keyboard's yellow MIDI OUT to Riff's MIDI IN.\nPlay: you hear the piano and the guitar together.\nTo hear only the guitar, set the keyboard's sound menu to None (MIDI only).",
  "guideRecipeGuitarResult": "Riff has no keys of its own: the keyboard sends it the notes.",
  "guideRecipeAmpTitle": "Put the guitar through the amp",
  "guideRecipeAmpSteps": "Tap + and pick Amp.\nIn the cable view, drag Riff's AUDIO OUT L to the Amp's AUDIO IN L, then R to R.\nPlay, and turn Drive on the Amp.",
  "guideRecipeAmpResult": "The clean guitar gets crunchy or distorted.",
  "guideRecipeControllerTitle": "Connect a MIDI controller",
  "guideRecipeControllerSteps": "Plug it in over USB (with an OTG adapter on a phone), or switch on a Bluetooth MIDI controller.\nOpen Preferences with the gear icon.\nUnder MIDI Connection, tap Connect MIDI Device and pick it.",
  "guideRecipeControllerResult": "It plays the module whose MIDI CH badge matches the channel it sends on, usually 1.",
  "guideRecipeLearnTitle": "Map a knob",
  "guideRecipeLearnSteps": "Tap the sliders icon at the top of a module.\nTap Learn next to a control, for example Palm mute.\nMove a knob or press a pad on your controller.",
  "guideRecipeLearnResult": "The control now follows your hardware. The mapping is saved with the project.",
  "guideRecipeDrumsTitle": "Start a drum beat",
  "guideRecipeDrumsSteps": "Tap + and pick Drum Generator.\nPick a pattern from the menu.\nSwitch Active on and press play at the top.",
  "guideRecipeDrumsResult": "The beat follows the tempo in the transport bar.",
  "guideRecipeLoopTitle": "Record a loop",
  "guideRecipeLoopSteps": "Tap + and pick Audio Looper.\nIn the cable view, cable the keyboard's AUDIO OUT L and R into the looper's AUDIO IN L and R.\nPress the looper's record button. Recording starts on the first beat of the next bar.\nPlay, then press it again: recording stops at the end of the bar and the loop plays. Press it once more to add a layer.",
  "guideRecipeLoopResult": "If the tempo was stopped, it starts and gives you one bar to get ready.",
  "guideRecipeProjectsTitle": "Save and open projects",
  "guideRecipeProjectsSteps": "Tap the folder icon at the top.\nSave As… writes your modules, cables and settings to a .gf file.\nNew Project starts over with a keyboard and Xen. Anything not saved is lost.\nOpen Project loads a saved file.",
  "guideRecipeProjectsResult": "The app also keeps your current session between launches, except in the web demo.",
  "guideModulesIntro": "Everything the + button at the bottom of the rack can add. Drag the handle on the left of a module to move it.",
  "guideVocoderNote": "Use wired headphones or speakers: Bluetooth adds too much delay to sing live.",
